@*
    The mark of a domain type: what a `.domain` file is, and what each chapter
    in it describes.

    Thirty-two glyphs on one 16x16 grid — the thirty-one distinct values of the
    contract-16 `.domain` sets, and one generic sheet for an additional page whose
    type is its own filename — built from three primitives so the set reads as a
    family rather than as thirty-two drawings. `requirements` and `invariants`
    are in both the chapter and the file set and mean the same thing at both
    levels, so each is one glyph. The relationships are the point and they have
    to survive any edit here:

      * a filled dot always means identity — an entity has one, a value object
        never does;
      * a diamond always means "defined by its value" — one for a value object,
        two overlapping for the shared ones;
      * a boundary always means one consistency unit — the rounded rectangle an
        aggregate draws around the things inside it.

    Read the set that way and `aggregate` is a boundary holding an identified
    thing and two plain ones, `entity` is a boundary with an identity dot in it,
    and `value-object` is a diamond with no dot anywhere. Redraw one of them
    freehand and that sentence stops being true, which is why the coordinates
    below are transcribed rather than authored.

    Drawn here rather than fetched, for the reason ProviderMark's header gives at
    length: a component that needs the network to show itself is no use in a
    WebView with no egress. So there is no sprite file, no icon font and no CDN —
    each glyph is shapes in this file and nothing downstream ships a second
    asset.

    Stroked at 1.6, never filled, which is the library's state-icon family rule
    and the one ProviderMark states: provider marks are filled and state icons are
    stroked at 1.6, so a reader never mistakes one class of thing for the other.
    The identity dots are the deliberate exception — a dot that is not filled is a
    hollow circle, which in this family already means something else.

    Two more idioms grew out of the three and are used the same way everywhere:
    a second copy drawn behind a shape means "the grouping of these" (shared
    enums, the actors file, the ubiquitous-language grouping), and a shape with a
    short list beside it means "the file, or chapter, that lists these" (features,
    skills, requirements, invariants). A new plural is drawn with one of the two,
    not with a third.

    Monochrome, and that is a rule rather than an omission. The set groups into
    families — Boundary, Structure, Behaviour, Capability, Rules, Actors,
    Language, and the files — and it is
    tempting to tint them. `.design/color-scheme.md` forbids it: a new language
    MUST map onto the existing tokens and MUST NOT add a colour, badge families
    get no per-value tone, and `color-band-1..5` is closed to a listed set of
    repository-identity consumers. So the families survive as grouping and
    headings on the storybook page and never as colour in the product; everything
    here is currentColor and inherits whatever ink it is sitting in.

    Naming and the tooltip are two parameters, not one, and that split is the
    reason this mark can lead a heading without costing anything. `role="img"` plus
    `aria-label` is an accessible name and adds no text node; a `<title>` is the
    hover tooltip and *is* a text node. So a chapter heading asks for the name and
    declines the tooltip: a listener still hears "type: aggregate", and the
    heading's textContent is byte for byte the title it always was. Bundling the
    two would have forced a choice between announcing the type and leaving the
    heading's text alone, and neither is worth giving up.

    The same textContent rule is why the shapes inside each arm are written joined
    — the closing `/>` of one on the line of the next. Razor trims whitespace
    around a code block but keeps it *between* two literal sibling elements, so one
    shape per line in the ordinary way would put five whitespace text nodes inside
    this `svg`. Joined tags emit none. Nothing to do with labelling; it is the
    `<title>` and this whitespace that are the only two ways this component can
    grow text, and both are switched off in a heading.

    Worth being honest about what that buys. Nothing in this repository derives a
    heading anchor from DOM textContent today — the `.domain` parse computes its
    own slugs from the markdown — so this is a property kept because it is cheap
    and because a mark has no business changing what a heading says, not a live
    dependency somebody would find by grepping. Keep the tags joined; the unit test
    named for it will say so if they come apart.

    An additional page — a file the convention does not name, whose `type` is
    its own filename — is recognised only with that filename beside it, which is
    what FileName is for, and draws the generic `page` sheet. The modifier class
    is the glyph's (`devbook-type-marker--page`); the accessible name stays the
    value the file states.

    An unrecognised value renders nothing at all. The `.domain` vocabulary grows,
    and a value set that grows must never make a page look broken — the caller
    keeps showing the plain word, and asks DevbookTypeMarkers.IsRecognised when
    it needs to know which of the two it got.

    Size is an em by default so the mark scales with the heading level it leads.
    `.design/typography-and-layout.md#iconography` asks for an explicit
    width/height rather than a font-size scale, and this is one — it is simply
    measured in the heading's own type. Chrome at a fixed density passes a px
    value the way the state icons do.
*@

@if (Slug is not null)
{
    <svg class="@ClassValue"
         viewBox="0 0 16 16"
         width="@Size"
         height="@Size"
         fill="none"
         stroke="currentColor"
         stroke-width="1.6"
         stroke-linecap="round"
         stroke-linejoin="round"
         role="@(Labelled ? "img" : null)"
         aria-label="@(Labelled ? Label : null)"
         aria-hidden="@(Labelled ? null : "true")"
         focusable="false"
         data-testid="@TestId"
         @attributes="AdditionalAttributes">
        @if (Labelled && ShowTooltip)
        {
            <title>@Label</title>
        }
        @* Boundary — the context itself, as the map addresses it. *@
        @if (Slug is "bounded-context")
        {
            @* The dashed boundary the domain file draws, with nothing modelled in
               it yet and one identity dot: the context as one addressable thing
               on the map. *@
            <rect x="1.5" y="2.4" width="13" height="11.2" rx="2.8" stroke-dasharray="2.4 2.2"
            /><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="1.7" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
        }
        @* Structure — what the model is made of. *@
        else if (Slug is "aggregate")
        {
            @* A boundary holding an identified thing and the two plain ones it
               owns: the consistency unit, drawn as exactly that. *@
            <rect x="1.6" y="2.9" width="12.8" height="10.2" rx="2.6"
            /><path d="M6.9 7.3 9.5 6.2"
            /><path d="M6.9 8.7 9.5 9.8"
            /><circle cx="5.4" cy="8" r="1.7" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"
            /><circle cx="10.7" cy="5.8" r="1.15"
            /><circle cx="10.7" cy="10.2" r="1.15" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "entity")
        {
            @* One boundary, one identity dot, and the fields under it. *@
            <rect x="2.5" y="2.5" width="11" height="11" rx="2.6"
            /><circle cx="5.7" cy="5.9" r="1.4" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"
            /><path d="M8.6 5.9h2.7"
            /><path d="M4.7 9.4h6.6"
            /><path d="M4.7 11.4h4.2" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "value-object")
        {
            @* A diamond inside a diamond and no dot anywhere: defined by its
               value, all the way down. *@
            <path d="M8 1.9 14.1 8 8 14.1 1.9 8Z"
            /><path d="M5.4 8 8 5.4 10.6 8 8 10.6Z" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "enum")
        {
            @* A closed list with one member picked out. *@
            <circle cx="3.6" cy="4.2" r="1.2"
            /><circle cx="3.6" cy="8" r="1.2" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"
            /><circle cx="3.6" cy="11.8" r="1.2"
            /><path d="M6.8 4.2h6M6.8 8h6M6.8 11.8h6" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "shared-value-objects")
        {
            @* Two diamonds overlapping: the value-object shape, held in common. *@
            <path d="M5.6 1.9 9.6 5.9 5.6 9.9 1.6 5.9Z"
            /><path d="M10.4 6.1 14.4 10.1 10.4 14.1 6.4 10.1Z" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "shared-enums")
        {
            @* The enum's list with a second copy of it behind. *@
            <path d="M5 2.3h6.9a1.8 1.8 0 0 1 1.8 1.8V11"
            /><rect x="1.9" y="4.9" width="9" height="9" rx="1.9"
            /><circle cx="4.7" cy="7.6" r="0.95" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"
            /><circle cx="4.7" cy="11" r="0.95"
            /><path d="M6.9 7.6h1.9M6.9 11h1.9" />
        }
        @* Behaviour — what the model does. *@
        else if (Slug is "domain-service")
        {
            @* Something in, something out, and a boundary in the middle doing the
               work. The only member of the set with both ends open. *@
            <rect x="4.2" y="3.9" width="8.2" height="8.2" rx="2.2"
            /><path d="M0.9 8h3.3"
            /><path d="M12.4 8h2.7"
            /><path d="M13.5 6.6 14.9 8l-1.4 1.4"
            /><path d="M6.6 8h3.4" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "domain-event")
        {
            @* The bolt: something already happened, and it travelled. *@
            <path d="M9.1 1.6 3.9 9.3h3.6l-.6 5.1 5.2-7.7H8.5Z" />
        }
        @* Capability — what the product offers. *@
        else if (Slug is "feature")
        {
            @* A flag on its pole. *@
            <path d="M3.6 14.2V2.1"
            /><path d="M3.6 2.6h8.3l-1.8 2.8 1.8 2.8H3.6" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "sub-feature")
        {
            @* The same flag, on a pole hanging off the one above it. *@
            <path d="M2.4 1.9v6.4a1.8 1.8 0 0 0 1.8 1.8h1.4"
            /><path d="M7.2 14.1V6.5"
            /><path d="M7.2 7h6.3l-1.4 2.1 1.4 2.1H7.2" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "feature-flag")
        {
            @* A switch: decided at release, and either on or off. The knob is
               hollow because a flag's position is configuration, not an
               identity or a member picked out of a list. *@
            <rect x="1.5" y="4.6" width="13" height="6.8" rx="3.4"
            /><circle cx="11.1" cy="8" r="1.8" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "setting")
        {
            @* Two sliders: a value a person moves at runtime, anywhere along its
               range rather than at one of two ends. *@
            <path d="M1.8 4.6h3.1M8.3 4.6h5.9"
            /><circle cx="6.6" cy="4.6" r="1.7"
            /><path d="M1.8 11.4h7.4M12.6 11.4h1.6"
            /><circle cx="10.9" cy="11.4" r="1.7" />
        }
        @* Rules — what is either kept or broken. *@
        else if (Slug is "requirement")
        {
            @* A box with a tick: one promise, and it is either kept or not. *@
            <rect x="2.3" y="2.3" width="11.4" height="11.4" rx="2.4"
            /><path d="M5.2 8.2l2 2 3.8-4.4" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "requirements")
        {
            @* The tick box with the list of them beside it — the features file's
               composition, because this is one feature's promises, listed. The
               same glyph at both levels: the rule gives the word one meaning at
               both. *@
            <rect x="1.6" y="1.6" width="6.8" height="6.8" rx="1.6"
            /><path d="M3.4 5.1l1.2 1.2 2.1-2.5"
            /><path d="M10.6 10.1h4M10.6 12.9h4"
            /><path d="M7.4 10.1h.9M7.4 12.9h.9" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "invariant")
        {
            @* A padlock: what the type will not let any caller break. *@
            <rect x="3" y="7" width="10" height="7" rx="1.8"
            /><path d="M5.4 7V5.2a2.6 2.6 0 0 1 5.2 0V7"
            /><path d="M8 9.8v1.6" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "invariants")
        {
            @* The padlock with the list of them beside it, the same composition as
               requirements, and the same glyph at both levels for the same
               reason. *@
            <rect x="1.6" y="4.6" width="6.8" height="4.8" rx="1.3"
            /><path d="M3.3 4.6V3.4a1.7 1.7 0 0 1 3.4 0v1.2"
            /><path d="M10.6 10.1h4M10.6 12.9h4"
            /><path d="M7.4 10.1h.9M7.4 12.9h.9" />
        }
        @* Actors — who issues the commands. *@
        else if (Slug is "user")
        {
            @* A person: an account that operates the context. *@
            <circle cx="8" cy="5.2" r="2.7"
            /><path d="M2.8 14.2a5.2 5.2 0 0 1 10.4 0" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "organisation")
        {
            @* A building: a body the context acts toward without operating it. *@
            <path d="M2.4 14V3.4a1.2 1.2 0 0 1 1.2-1.2h5.2a1.2 1.2 0 0 1 1.2 1.2V14"
            /><path d="M10 6.6h2.4a1.2 1.2 0 0 1 1.2 1.2V14"
            /><path d="M1.2 14h13.6"
            /><path d="M4.8 5.2h1.6M4.8 8h1.6M4.8 10.8h1.6" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "technical")
        {
            @* A clock: a system or timer that triggers a use case from outside. *@
            <circle cx="8" cy="8" r="6.2"
            /><path d="M8 4.6V8l2.4 1.6" />
        }
        @* Language — what the words mean. *@
        else if (Slug is "term")
        {
            @* A speech bubble with a definition in it. *@
            <rect x="1.9" y="2.4" width="12.2" height="9.2" rx="2.3"
            /><path d="M5.5 11.6v2.7l3.3-2.7"
            /><path d="M5.1 5.7h5.8M5.1 8.3h3.4" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "ubiquitous-language")
        {
            @* The term's bubble with a second copy behind it: the grouping that
               holds the terms, drawn with the same "more than one" the shared
               enums draw. *@
            <path d="M5 1.8h7.3a1.8 1.8 0 0 1 1.8 1.8v5.6"
            /><rect x="1.9" y="4.4" width="10" height="7.6" rx="2"
            /><path d="M4.8 12v2.4l2.9-2.4"
            /><path d="M4.6 7.4h4.6M4.6 9.6h2.6" />
        }
        @* The files a bounded context is written across. requirements and
           invariants are drawn above, once for both levels. *@
        else if (Slug is "context-map")
        {
            @* Three contexts and the relationships between them. *@
            <circle cx="3.6" cy="4" r="1.9"
            /><circle cx="12.4" cy="4" r="1.9"
            /><circle cx="8" cy="12" r="1.9"
            /><path d="M5.5 4h5"
            /><path d="M4.6 5.7l2.4 4.6"
            /><path d="M11.4 5.7 9 10.3" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "domain")
        {
            @* A dashed boundary — the context — with the model inside it. *@
            <rect x="1.5" y="2.4" width="13" height="11.2" rx="2.8" stroke-dasharray="2.4 2.2"
            /><rect x="4.9" y="5.8" width="6.2" height="4.4" rx="1.5" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "model")
        {
            @* A table with a header row: structure, tabulated. *@
            <rect x="2.1" y="2.5" width="11.8" height="11" rx="1.9"
            /><path d="M2.1 6.2h11.8"
            /><path d="M4.5 8.7h6.9M4.5 11h4.4" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "features")
        {
            @* The feature flag, with the list of them beside it. *@
            <path d="M2.6 13.9V2.4"
            /><path d="M2.6 2.9h5.9l-1.3 2 1.3 2H2.6"
            /><path d="M10.6 10.1h4M10.6 12.9h4"
            /><path d="M7.4 10.1h.9M7.4 12.9h.9" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "flow")
        {
            @* Two chevrons: one step after another. *@
            <path d="M3.2 3.4 7.3 8l-4.1 4.6"
            /><path d="M8.9 3.4 13 8l-4.1 4.6" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "dependencies")
        {
            @* One box pointing at another. *@
            <rect x="1.5" y="1.9" width="6.2" height="4.6" rx="1.5"
            /><rect x="8.3" y="9.5" width="6.2" height="4.6" rx="1.5"
            /><path d="M4.6 6.5v3.5a1.8 1.8 0 0 0 1.8 1.8h1.9"
            /><path d="M7.1 10.5 8.4 11.8 7.1 13.1" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "context")
        {
            @* The dashed boundary again, holding the prose that says where it
               runs: the context's root document is the boundary, written down. *@
            <rect x="1.5" y="2.4" width="13" height="11.2" rx="2.8" stroke-dasharray="2.4 2.2"
            /><path d="M4.6 6.4h6.8"
            /><path d="M4.6 9.6h4.6" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "actors")
        {
            @* The user's silhouette with a second one behind it: the file that
               holds all of them. *@
            <circle cx="6.2" cy="5.6" r="2.4"
            /><path d="M1.6 14a4.6 4.6 0 0 1 9.2 0"
            /><path d="M10.2 3.4a2.4 2.4 0 0 1 0 4.5"
            /><path d="M12.2 9.6a4.6 4.6 0 0 1 2.4 4.4" />
        }
        else if (Slug is "skills")
        {
            @* The features file's composition with a run mark in the flag's
               place: capabilities that are procedures, listed. *@
            <path d="M2.4 2.3v6.4l5.1-3.2Z"
            /><path d="M10.6 10.1h4M10.6 12.9h4"
            /><path d="M7.4 10.1h.9M7.4 12.9h.9" />
        }
        @* An additional page: a file the convention does not name, whose type is
           its own filename. One generic sheet for all of them, because the
           filename is the only thing that tells them apart and the label already
           carries it. *@
        else if (Slug is "page")
        {
            <path d="M3.4 1.8h6l3.2 3.2v9.2H3.4Z"
            /><path d="M9.4 1.8V5h3.2"
            /><path d="M5.6 8.6h4.8M5.6 11.2h3" />
        }
    </svg>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The <c>type</c> value exactly as the file states it. A value the
    /// set has never heard of renders nothing, so a caller may write this
    /// unconditionally beside a word it is still showing.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string? Value { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Names the mark to assistive technology, and only then — the same
    /// default ProviderMark takes and for the same reason: a mark beside its own
    /// text label would otherwise be announced twice. The caller that has taken
    /// the word off the screen is the caller that passes this.
    /// <para>This is <c>role="img"</c> and an <c>aria-label</c>, and nothing else.
    /// It adds no text node, so naming the mark is free wherever it is drawn —
    /// including in front of a heading whose text must not move.</para></summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Labelled { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether a named mark also carries a <c>title</c>, which is the
    /// pointer user's tooltip.
    /// <para>Separate from <see cref="Labelled"/> because the two cost different
    /// things. The accessible name is an attribute; the tooltip is an element with
    /// text in it, and text inside a heading's mark is text the heading now
    /// contains. On by default, so a mark that is named is discoverable by hover
    /// as well; a heading turns it off and keeps the name.</para>
    /// <para>Coupled to <see cref="Labelled"/> rather than free of it: a tooltip on
    /// a mark hidden from assistive technology would be a fact only a mouse could
    /// reach. That rule holds wherever it is invoked, which is worth more than a
    /// knob for the one case that might want to bend it — a decorative mark beside
    /// a visible label does not need the tooltip either, because the label is
    /// already the word.</para></summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool ShowTooltip { get; set; } = true;

    /// <summary>Edge length. An em by default, so the mark is the same size
    /// relative to whatever heading it leads — an <c>h3</c>'s mark and an
    /// <c>h4</c>'s are then one mark rather than two weights of it. Chrome at a
    /// fixed density passes a px value instead.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string Size { get; set; } = "0.82em";

    [Parameter]
    public string? CssClass { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? TestId { get; set; }

    [Parameter(CaptureUnmatchedValues = true)]
    public IReadOnlyDictionary<string, object>? AdditionalAttributes { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The file the value was read from, for a mark drawn on a file. Only
    /// needed for an additional <c>.domain</c> page, whose <c>type</c> is its own
    /// filename and so is known only beside that name — see
    /// <see cref="DevbookTypeMarkers.IsAdditionalPage"/>. A chapter's mark leaves
    /// it out, and a closed-set value draws the same with or without it.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? FileName { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Which glyph to draw, or nothing — computed once per render, since
    /// the arms below ask it for every branch.</summary>
    private string? Slug { get; set; }

    protected override void OnParametersSet() => Slug = DevbookTypeMarkers.GlyphFor(Value, FileName);

    /// <summary>The field and its value together, which is what the metadata row
    /// this mark replaces used to read. Announcing only "aggregate" would leave a
    /// listener working out which of a chapter's fields had become a picture.
    /// The value as written rather than the glyph's slug: an additional page is
    /// "type: regulatory-annex", which is what its file says, not a "page" nobody
    /// wrote.</summary>
    private string Label => $"type: {DevbookTypeMarkers.Normalise(Value!)}";

    private string ClassValue
    {
        get
        {
            var mark = $"devbook-type-marker devbook-type-marker--{Slug}";
            return string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(CssClass) ? mark : $"{mark} {CssClass}";
        }
    }
}
